In the `eval` method, the variable `allBlocksAreNulls` is set to `false` if any value in `valuesBlock` is non-null for a given position `p`. However, this logic can be simplified by using a logical OR operation directly within the condition. This avoids unnecessary assignment and makes the code more concise:
```java
if (valuesBlock.isNull(p)) {
    allBlocksAreNulls = true;
} else {
    allBlocksAreNulls = false;
}
```
can be replaced with:
```java
allBlocksAreNulls |= !valuesBlock.isNull(p);
```

